# apps/web
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# The anon (publishable, sb_publishable_...) key. Vercel names it SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;
# apps/web/next.config.ts copies it into the browser build as NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.
# Either name works locally.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# PUUID of the first admin. The API calls public.bootstrap_admin(puuid) with it on start
# (M1.5/M1.6): inserts the player row if the PUUID is new, sets is_admin either way.
# Idempotent, so it can stay set.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PUUID=
# Discord user id (snowflake) to link to BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PUUID, once. Optional but needed for
# the very first sign-in: /admin matches a session to a player by players.discord_id, and the
# bootstrap admin is seeded by PUUID, so without this nobody can get in to do the linking.
# Idempotent, and it never moves a link that already exists. Right-click yourself in Discord
# with developer mode on -> Copy User ID.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_DISCORD_ID=
# Origin OAuth comes back to, e.g. https://customs.example. Optional locally (the request's own
# host is used); pin it on Vercel so the redirect and the Supabase allow-list agree.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# IANA timezone a night is measured in (M2.5). A night runs 06:00 to 06:00 there, which is what
# "games tonight" counts over for the sit-out rotation. Optional; defaults to Africa/Cairo.
CUSTOMS_NIGHT_TZ=
# Optional bearer token for the three scheduled routes. GET /api/cron/sweep is the scheduled half
# of the 2-hour idle sweep (a lobby nobody has posted about in two hours becomes `abandoned`);
# the sweep also runs at the start of every companion post, so that half is only for the night
# everybody closed the client and nothing will post again. GET /api/cron/leaderboard posts the
# nightly board to the Discord webhook (M3.5) and has no other trigger: whatever calls it decides
# what time the board lands. GET /api/cron/window posts the closed week, and on the 1st the closed
# month (M5.13); it is safe at any cadence because it posts a window exactly once whatever calls
# it. Unset, all three answer 503 and are closed. Any long random string.
#
# WHO CALLS THEM: Vercel Cron, from apps/web/vercel.json -- the leaderboard and the window both at
# `30 4 * * *`, i.e. 04:30 UTC, which is 07:30 in Cairo in summer and 06:30 in winter and so is
# always after the 06:00 night boundary. Daily, because the Hobby plan allows one run a day per
# cron; both routes are safe at any cadence, so a paid plan can simply tighten the schedule.
# **Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` by itself when this variable is set on the
# project** -- that is the same door these routes already check, so nothing else has to be
# configured. Set it in the Vercel project's environment variables (Production), not only here.
# The sweep has no cron entry: it runs at the start of every companion post.
CRON_SECRET=
# The operator (M13.6 / M14.19): comma-separated Supabase auth user ids (auth.users.id, a uuid --
# Supabase dashboard -> Authentication -> Users) who may READ any group: every admin GET and admin
# page, read-only, with the invite link masked, plus GET /api/ops/groups and the /ops page. Never a
# write: every admin POST stays group-admin only. Not stored anywhere else -- no row, column or
# migration names them; changing it is a deploy. Unset or empty: nobody is an operator and
# /api/ops/groups is 403 for everyone. Server only; set it on Vercel (Production) too.
SUPER_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# Supabase Auth Discord provider (read by the Supabase CLI from packages/db/supabase/config.toml,
# NOT by the web app). Local stack only: on the hosted project these go in the dashboard.
# See apps/web/README.md for the Discord developer portal steps and the redirect URLs.
SUPABASE_AUTH_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
SUPABASE_AUTH_DISCORD_SECRET=
# Connect Discord in one click (M14.20): OAuth2 `webhook.incoming` on the SAME Discord application
# as sign-in. Copy the id and secret from SUPABASE_AUTH_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID / _SECRET above (those
# two are read by the Supabase CLI only; hosted sign-in lives in the Supabase dashboard, so the web
# server needs its own copy, here and on Vercel). Server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Unset: `Connect Discord` sends the admin back with the paste-a-webhook fallback; nothing else
# changes. The secret also keys the HMAC on the OAuth `state`, so rotating it voids states in flight
# (ten minutes' worth at most).
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional. The exact callback registered under the application's OAuth2 -> Redirects in the Discord
# developer portal; Discord compares it character for character. Unset, it is
# <site origin>/api/admin/discord/callback. Locally: http://localhost:3000/api/admin/discord/callback.
DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI=
# Kustom Premium's AI lines (M16.3): the Anthropic API key, from the Anthropic console. Server only,
# never NEXT_PUBLIC_; read by apps/web/lib/ai/client.ts and nothing else. Set it on Vercel
# **Production** only (not Preview, so preview deploys never spend), and in apps/web/.env.local only
# to try AI lines locally. Also set a $20 monthly spend limit in the Anthropic console: it backs up
# Kustom's own meter ($2 per group, $20 overall, table ai_settings). Unset or blank: every AI path is
# silently absent (no call, no line, no error) and nothing else changes. The operator's kill switch
# needs no deploy: `update public.ai_settings set calls_enabled = false;` in the Supabase SQL editor.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Kustom Premium's AI on DeepSeek's own API (the user's 2026-10-04 move; data is processed in the
# PRC, which the user accepted): the DeepSeek API key, from platform.deepseek.com -> API keys. Server
# only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_; read by apps/web/lib/ai/client.ts and nothing else (it calls
# https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic with the same Anthropic SDK). Vercel **Production** only.
# Model: deepseek-v4-pro for all three lines (lib/ai/meter.ts). The same meter, caps and kill switch.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Which provider writes the AI lines: deepseek or anthropic. Set, it uses only that provider's key
# (no key = AI off; a typo = AI off). Unset: the preferred provider (deepseek, the owner's
# 2026-10-04 call) if its key is set, else whichever key is set. Set it to anthropic (or remove
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY) on Vercel Production to fall back to Claude.
AI_PROVIDER=
# Test only, never on Vercel: with an AI key set AND this set to 1, `pnpm --filter web exec
# vitest run lib/ai/live.test.ts` makes one real call on the provider's game model (well under
# $0.01). CI never sets either.
KUSTOM_AI_LIVE=
# Test only, never on Vercel (M18.5): the path of the production rating export the M18.3 replay
# reads in place (`lib/ingest/kustomReplay.test.ts`). Unset, the test skips; never in CI.
KUSTOM_REPLAY_CSV=
# packages/db integration tests (optional).
# They ask the Supabase CLI for the local stack's URL and keys and skip when it is not
# running. Set these three only to point the tests somewhere else; never at production.
SUPABASE_LOCAL_URL=
SUPABASE_LOCAL_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_LOCAL_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# The stack's JWT secret: M14.5's RLS tests sign real session tokens with it. Set it whenever
# you set the three above (they fail without it); otherwise the CLI supplies it too.
SUPABASE_LOCAL_JWT_SECRET=
# apps/companion reads no .env file: its config is <configDir>/config.json ({ apiBase, companionToken,
# lockfilePath? }, written by the first-run prompt with owner-only permissions). Process environment only:
#   CUSTOMS_NIGHT_CONFIG_DIR   override the config directory (default %APPDATA%\customs-night on Windows,
#                              ~/Library/Application Support/customs-night on macOS, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/customs-night on Linux)
#   CUSTOMS_NIGHT_LOG_LEVEL    console level: debug | info | warn | error (default info; the log file always gets debug)
#   LCU_LOCKFILE_CANDIDATES    from @customs/lcu: replaces the default lockfile paths (tests/CI only)
#
# Release build only (`pnpm --filter companion build:win` / `release`, never the exe itself). Optional: bake a
# different API origin into the exe (default https://playkustom.com). Publishing uses the `gh` CLI's
# own login (GitHub release on suyaser/kustom-releases); there is no token variable.
CUSTOMS_NIGHT_API_BASE=
